          "text": "DermaSensor Inc. - Company ProfileSolutionsIndustriesServicesResourcesAboutCompany Directory > MedTech > DermaSensor Inc.⚠Is this information incorrect? This profile was AI-generated from publicly available sources and may contain errors. If you are a representative of DermaSensor Inc. and believe any information on this page is inaccurate, we will promptly correct or remove it.REPORT AN ERRORDermaSensor Inc. ↗Miami, USAVISIT WEBSITEDermaSensor Inc. is a health technology company that has developed the first FDA-cleared, AI-powered medical device for the non-invasive detection of the three most common skin cancers: melanoma, basal cell carcinoma, and squamous cell carcinoma. The handheld device utilizes Elastic Scattering Spectroscopy (ESS) and proprietary machine learning algorithms to analyze skin lesions at cellular and subcellular levels, providing immediate, objective results at the point of care. Headquartered in Miami, Florida, the company focuses on empowering primary care physicians (PCPs) to better evaluate suspicious skin lesions, addressing a significant gap in dermatology access. By providing a 'point and click' diagnostic tool, DermaSensor aims to improve early detection rates and optimize the referral process to specialists, potentially saving lives through earlier intervention in skin cancer cases.CLASSIFICATIONCompany Type:MedTechTherapeutic Areas:OncologyDermatologyIndustry:Medical DevicesSub-Industry:AI-powered DiagnosticsSIZE & FINANCIALSEmployees:1-50Revenue:$1M-$10MFounded:2009Ownership:privateStatus:operatingFUNDINGStage:Series BTotal Raised:$60.7MInvestors:SternAegis Ventures, Ceros Capital Markets, Pier 70 Ventures, Kern Venture Group, GenHenn Capital, Healthtech Capital, LSP, Miami AngelsPIPELINEStage:CommercialLead Drug Stage:Commercial (Medical Device)Modalities:AI-powered Optical Spectroscopy, Elastic Scattering Spectroscopy (ESS)Active Trials:3Trial Phases:Phase 3: 1FDA Approvals:1EMA Approvals:1CORPORATE STRUCTUREKey